[{"id":126160,"sender_id":1002,"sender_full_name":"perezl.alonso","avatar_url":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/b47e415ea36ec5eb3afc8f0a568e2a5c?d=identicon&version=1","content":"<p><a href=\"#narrow/channel/2-Latest-Changes/topic/gauged.20WZW.20model/near/126160\">#6</a> On the same topic as <a href=\"#narrow/channel/2-Latest-Changes/topic/gauged.20WZW.20model/near/122372\">#4</a>, is there a citeable article for the observations that gauged WZW models are sigma models valued in the action groupoid <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>G</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">/</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">/</mi><mi>H</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">G//H</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">G</span><span class=\"mord\">//</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0813em;\">H</span></span></span></span> with connections (meaning fields are connections on smooth groupoid bundles), such that the topological term is a gerbe <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>G</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">/</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">/</mi><mi>H</mi><msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">∇</mi></msub><mo>→</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant=\"bold\">B</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">∇</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mi>U</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">(G//H)_{\\nabla} \\to \\mathbf{B}^2 _{\\nabla} U(1)</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">G</span><span class=\"mord\">//</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0813em;\">H</span><span class=\"mclose\"><span class=\"mclose\">)</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.3283em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:0em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">∇</span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.15em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">→</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:1.0894em;vertical-align:-0.2753em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathbf\">B</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.8141em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.4247em;margin-left:0em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">∇</span></span></span></span><span style=\"top:-3.063em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">2</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.2753em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.109em;\">U</span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord\">1</span><span class=\"mclose\">)</span></span></span></span> There is the equivariant picture in the nLab page of course but I ask about the direct (or almost) direct statements.</p>","timestamp":1791036619,"subject":"gauged WZW model","stream_id":2,"display_recipient":"Latest Changes","reactions":[]},{"id":126161,"sender_id":11,"sender_full_name":"Urs","avatar_url":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/b00d1ee17463af676c78974439b92471?d=identicon&version=1","content":"<p><a href=\"#narrow/channel/2-Latest-Changes/topic/gauged.20WZW.20model/near/126161\">#7</a> Maybe Thm. 4.16 in:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><a href=\"https://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/Byungdo%20Park\">Byungdo Park</a>, <a href=\"https://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/Corbett%20Redden\">Corbett Redden</a>: <em>A classification of equivariant gerbe connections</em>, Communications in Contemporary Mathematics <strong>21</strong> 02 (2019) 1850001 [<a href=\"https://doi.org/10.1142/S0219199718500013\">doi:10.1142/S0219199718500013</a>, <a href=\"https://arxiv.org/abs/1709.06003\">arXiv:1709.06003</a>]</li>\n</ul>","timestamp":1791046713,"subject":"gauged WZW model","stream_id":2,"display_recipient":"Latest Changes","reactions":[]},{"id":126164,"sender_id":1002,"sender_full_name":"perezl.alonso","avatar_url":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/b47e415ea36ec5eb3afc8f0a568e2a5c?d=identicon&version=1","content":"<p><a href=\"#narrow/channel/2-Latest-Changes/topic/gauged.20WZW.20model/near/126164\">#8</a> Ah great, also Section 5.2. I don’t see a definition of <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>E</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">∇</mi></msub><mi>G</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">E_{\\nabla}G</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.8333em;vertical-align:-0.15em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0576em;\">E</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.3283em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:-0.0576em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">∇</span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.15em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">G</span></span></span></span> though, I assume that should be the moduli stack of principal <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>G</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">/</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">/</mi><mi>G</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">G//G</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">G</span><span class=\"mord\">//</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">G</span></span></span></span> smooth groupoid bundles with connection for <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>G</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">/</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">/</mi><mi>G</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">G//G</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">G</span><span class=\"mord\">//</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">G</span></span></span></span> the left translation action groupoid?</p>","timestamp":1791060984,"subject":"gauged WZW model","stream_id":2,"display_recipient":"Latest Changes","reactions":[]},{"id":126168,"sender_id":11,"sender_full_name":"Urs","avatar_url":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/b00d1ee17463af676c78974439b92471?d=identicon&version=1","content":"<p><a href=\"#narrow/channel/2-Latest-Changes/topic/gauged.20WZW.20model/near/126168\">#9</a> If you find it worthwhile, consider a small community service and put a corresponding note into this <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">n</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.4306em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">n</span></span></span></span>Lab entry!</p>","timestamp":1791096185,"subject":"gauged WZW model","stream_id":2,"display_recipient":"Latest Changes","reactions":[]}]